CON-03: add upstream run-on to LID units only when they fill the subcatchment

lid_getRunoff() added the subcatchment's run-on rate to every LID unit's
inflow when area >= lidArea, which is always true. subcatch_addRunonFlow()
already spreads the run-on over the non-LID area and books it there, so a
LID that covers only part of the subcatchment received the run-on a second
time, without a source in the water balance. Restore the 5.2.4 test
(area == lidArea; validateLidGroup() sets lidArea to area within 0.1 %), which
is what the comment above it says.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-03_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
index e2ac45a..edc8839 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
@@ -1711,7 +1711,7 @@ void lid_getRunoff(int j, double tStep)
             }
 
             // ... add upstream runon only if LID occupies full subcatchment
-            if (subcatch->area >= subcatch->lidArea)
+            if (subcatch->area == subcatch->lidArea)
             {
                 lidInflow += subcatch->runon;
             }
